  m_text: "One of the largest land mammals that ever walked the Earth \u2014 twice
    the weight of an average African elephant. Its tusks were overgrown incisors,
    not canines, and they were longer than those of any elephant alive today.\n\nIt
    ranged across Europe, Central Asia and the Middle East, favouring warm, humid
    country close to forest. The species appeared some 700\u2013800 thousand years
    ago and died out around 30 thousand years ago."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: b764d2234ba2d4856b64b76c920bd096, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -5740928937063029901, guid: b764d2234ba2d4856b64b76c920bd096, type: 2}
